Android, WebGL, macOS and iOS retain the 2026-09-01 manual GitHub Actions builds
(.github/workflows/build-natives.yml, precision "both"). Their managed TriangleMesh.Create
entry point now validates bounds and degenerate/welded-away triangles before native calls.
All future builds apply the mesh cleanup fix through glue/CMakeLists.txt without editing the
source checkout. Native API users on the older builds must rebuild to get that cleanup.

Unity glue (glue/box3d_unity_glue.c, b3u_* exports, GLUE VERSION 1): compiled into every binary
via glue/CMakeLists.txt since 2026-09-01 — the C# Burst paths (queries, events, body accessors)
require it and World.Create probes b3u_GlueVersion at startup. Every shipped binary above carries
the glue; a binary built without it logs the stale-glue error and the rerouted APIs throw
EntryPointNotFoundException.

On version bumps: update this file, rebuild ALL platforms, regenerate bindings, run struct-size tests.
